{"name":"Easter Orchid","hex":"#e6e1e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"easter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Eastern. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","comparative form of east: more east"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An easterly wind (a wind blowing from the east); especially, a strong one; a storm of such winds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/easter"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Easter orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Easter orchid is the common name of one of three fragrant orchids:"},{"items":["Cattleya mossiae, a native of Venezuela","Cattleya schroederae, a native of Colombia","Earina autumnalis, a native of New Zealand"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Cattleya_mossiae_-_Orqu%C3%ADdea_Nacional_Venezolana.jpg/330px-Cattleya_mossiae_-_Orqu%C3%ADdea_Nacional_Venezolana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter_orchid"},{"title":"Easter","blocks":[{"text":"Easter, also called Pasch or Pascha or Resurrection Sunday, is a Christian celebration and cultural holiday commemorating the resurrection of Jesus from the dead, described in the Bible's New Testament as having occurred on the third day of his burial following his crucifixion by the Romans at Calvary c. 30 AD. It is the culmination of the Passion of Jesus, preceded by Lent, a 40-day period of fasting, prayer, and penance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Chora_Anastasis2.jpg/330px-Chora_Anastasis2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cattleya_schroederae_-_Flickr._003.jpg/330px-Cattleya_schroederae_-_Flickr._003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cattleya_schroederae_-_Flickr._003.jpg/960px-Cattleya_schroederae_-_Flickr._003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u